  "decision_target_date": "06/11/2025",
  "decision_agency": "Borough",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;By reason of the inadequate provision of cycle parking storage which is safe, secure and accessible for all, the proposed development would fail to meet cycle parking standards as required by Policy LP42 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot; size=&quot;2&quot;&gt;By reason of the inadequate size of the proposed bedrooms, no outlook for bedrooms 5 and 6, it failing to have been sufficiently demonstrated that the proposed bedrooms would receive adequate levels of natural daylight, and the communal spaces failing to be of a high standard to provide primary functions and encourage social amenity, the proposal&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;would result in poor and substandard form of accommodation, detrimental to the living conditions of future occupiers. The proposed development would, therefore, conflict&amp;nbsp;with Policies LP2 and LP22 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a Unilateral Undertaking or a Section 106 Agreement to secure appropriate rent levels in accordance with the Local Housing Allowance, the development would fail to secure the proposed House in Multiple Occupation at an affordable rent level, contrary to Policy LP22 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a Unilateral Undertaking or a Section 106 Agreement securing appropriate mitigation by restricting future occupiers of the development from obtaining parking permits within the Controlled Parking Zone, the proposed development would likely exacerbate existing parking stress and congestion on the surrounding highway network. The development would, therefore, be contrary to Policy LP45 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020) and Policy T6 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
  "appeal_decision": null
}